    <!--
      On-screen keyboard. Narrow keys, tall keys: the widest row is ten of them
      and it shares the screen with the results grid, so width is the scarce
      dimension and height is free.

        10 x (30 + 2*2) + 12 padding + 16 side padding = 368dp

      The narrowest real TV is 720p at density 1.5, i.e. 853dp wide, leaving the
      keyboard column ~382dp at weight 1.3. Fits there and everywhere larger.

      No screen-size qualifiers: `sw` buckets key off the SHORTER edge, and a
      1080p TV is only 540dp tall, so every panel lands in the same bucket.
    -->
    <dimen name="tv_keyboard_key_w">30dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tv_keyboard_key_h">44dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tv_keyboard_key_wide">54dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tv_keyboard_key_space">136dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tv_keyboard_key_gap">2dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="tv_keyboard_key_text">18sp</dimen>
